Nf7 22. Nb3 $2 { Hoping for Na5-c6, but this knight only diverts White’s queen onto a bad square. } ( { Better was } 22. Qb1 Bh6 23. Qd3 { preventing } Be3 { , with roughly level chances. } ) 
a5 $1 { Preventing 23.Na5. } 23. Qa4 $2 { Another questionable move; what is the queen useful for here? } ( { If } 23. Nxc5 dxc5 24. Qxc5 g5 25. Bf2 Ng6 { White’s pawns are not threatening enough to fully compensate for the piece. } ) 
 ( { Healthier was } 23. Nd2 Bh6 24. Qb2 { accepting the previous mistakes and returning the queen to the defence, though after } Be3 25. Bf2 Bxf2 ( { or } 25. Qa4 Bd4 $5 ) 
26. Rxf2 f4 { Black will gain a promising kingside attack after ...g6-g5-g4 . } ) 
Bh6 24. Bf2 ( { Capturing the a5-pawn with } 24. Nb5 Be3 25. Kh1 g5 26. Be1 f4 27. Bxa5 Qe8 { leaves White’s pieces tied up and after } 28. Bd1 Nd8 ( { launching an attack with } 28. Bf2 h5 $5 { should work too } ) 
29. Nc3 Bd7 30. Nb5 Nb7 { Black is winning a piece. } ) 
