Nf6 { (threatening ...Ng4) } 28. Bh4 { This is refuted by } Be3 $1 29. Kh1 Ng5 30. Rae1 Ng4 { with a decisive attack. After } 31. Bg3 Bf4 $1 32. Bxf4 Rxf4 33. Rxf4 exf4 { once again, White’s queen is useless on a4 . } ) 
26. exf5 { White is essentially being forced to capture this pawn, as Black would follow up with 26...Nf6, further pressuring the e4-pawn. } ( { If } 26. Bd3 fxe4 $5 27. Bxe4 ( 27. fxe4 Nf6 { transposes to 25...fxe4 which is analyzed above; } 28. Kh1 Ng4 ) 
