 ( 30. Kh1 { doesn’t help: } Bf4 31. Nd3 Bxh2 $1 32. Kxh2 Qg5 { With a winning attack: } 33. Ne1 Nf4 34. g3 Qh6 35. Kg1 Ng5 $1 { A picturesque win for Black. } ) 
Qg5 31. g3 ( { More stubborn was } 31. Ne1 { but after } Qg7 $1 { White is defenceless against the threat of ...Bf4xh2 . For example: } 32. Kh1 ( { or } 32. Rb1 Bf4 33. Rb7 Bxh2 34. Kxh2 Nf4 { threatening ...Qh6 and ...Nh3 winning: } 35. g3 Qh6 36. Kg1 Ng5 $1 ) 
